Methodological and validation credits
-------------------------------------
The decomposition methods are credited in the function help pages and
README. Their authors are distinct from the authors of this R package.

R/wvw_decomp.R follows Wagstaff, van Doorslaer, and Watanabe (2003).
O'Donnell, van Doorslaer, Wagstaff, and Lindelow (2008), Analyzing Health
Equity Using Household Survey Data, Chapter 13, and its AHE13.do example
served as implementation references.
https://doi.org/10.1596/978-0-8213-6933-3

Validation comparisons used rineq 0.3.0 (Brecht Devleesschauwer, Saveria
Willimès, Carine Van Malderen, Peter Konings, Niko Speybroeck, and Kaspar
Meili) and conindex 1.7 (Owen O'Donnell, Stephen O'Neill, Tom Van Ourti,
and Brendan Walsh). These are credited as comparison tools; their source
code and reference datasets are not bundled with lunadecomp.
https://doi.org/10.32614/CRAN.package.rineq
https://www.stata-journal.com/article.html?article=st0427

R/ke_decomp.R implements the direct-regression approach of Roselinde
Kessels and Guido Erreygers (2019). Its covariance and survey extensions
are documented separately from the article's method.
https://doi.org/10.1002/hec.3891

Survey calculations use survey (Thomas Lumley) and svrep (Benjamin
Schneider). Other dependencies are listed in DESCRIPTION and retain
their respective licenses and authorship.

The bundled lunadecomp_example dataset is simulated for package examples
and tests. It is not the World Bank reference dataset.
